{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And the eyes of Israel, etc.</b> One needs to know why this information is written in this place, and what connection and relevance this matter has to what follows it: ״וַיִּשַּׁק לָהֶם וַיְחַבֵּק לָהֶם״. Further, one needs to examine its saying <b>lahem</b>, for it should have said ״וַיִּשַּׁק אוֹתָם״. And perhaps these two fine points each resolve its fellow: for inasmuch as his eyes had grown heavy with old age, he would embrace not in the proper place of embracing and kiss not in the proper place of kissing. Therefore it says ״lahem״ and did not say ״otam״. Understand this."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:49:57.387955308Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}